exagon $ABCDEF$, as shown. What is the perimeter of hexagon $\\allowbreak ABCDEF$?\n\n[asy]\nunitsize (0.1 cm);\n\ndraw((16,-20)--(-3,-20)--(0,0)--(-3,20)--(16,20));\ndraw((0,0)--(16,0));\ndraw((5,20)--(8,0)--(5,-20));\ndraw((13,20)--(16,0)--(13,-20));\ndot((18,0));\ndot((20,0));\ndot((22,0));\ndraw((24,0)--(50,0));\ndraw((23,20)--(47,20)--(50,0)--(47,-20)--(21,-20));\ndraw((23,20)--(26,0)--(23,-20));\ndraw((31,20)--(34,0)--(31,-20));\ndraw((39,20)--(42,0)--(39,-20));\ndraw((39,21)--(39,25));\ndraw((47,21)--(47,25));\ndraw((39,23)--(47,23));\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-3,20),NW);\nlabel(\"$B$\",(47,20),NE);\nlabel(\"$C$\",(50,0),E);\nlabel(\"$D$\",(47,-20),SE);\nlabel(\"$E$\",(-3,-20),SW);\nlabel(\"$F$\",(0,0),W);\nlabel(\"20'\",(43,23),N);\nlabel(\"62'\",(49,10),E);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"7a34714dd2e3263ab8cafce5a5896ace6c470b2b428e577071a5eb4945cbf613"},"seconds":15.215295553207397,"seed":828096569768017735,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the perimeter of hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\), we need to understand the structure of the chevron pattern formed by the parallelograms and how their sides contribute to the perimeter of the hexagon.\n\nEach parallelogram has sides of lengths 62 feet and 20 feet. The chevron pattern is such that the parallelograms are placed in a way that their sides of 20 feet form the sides of the hexagon.\n\n1. **Identify the sides contributing to the perimeter:**\n   - The hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\) is formed by the sides of length 20 feet of the parallelograms.\n   - There are 6 sides of the hexagon, each equal to 20 feet.\n\n2. **Calculate the perimeter:**\n   - Since each side of the hexagon is 20 feet and there are 6 sides, the perimeter \\(P\\) is given by:\n     \\[\n     P = 6 \\times 20 = 120 \\text{ feet}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\) is \\(\\boxed{120}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{120}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
